 ### [Null-Scattering Extension](4371-null-scattering-extension.md)
-Generalizes the equation of transfer to enable unbiased sampling from a modified transmittance equation using a constant majorant extinction coefficient. Solves efficient sampling in sparse or heterogeneous media by homogenizing density. Differs from standard delta tracking by maintaining $T_{maj}$ and applying Russian Roulette based on null density ratio. Choose when media density varies significantly along rays and standard tracking becomes inefficient.
+Generalizes the equation of transfer to enable unbiased sampling from a modified transmittance equation using a constant majorant extinction coefficient. It solves the problem of efficiently sampling interaction points in sparse or heterogeneous media by homogenizing the density to a fixed majorant $\sigma_{maj}$, allowing algorithms like delta tracking to function correctly. It transforms the integro-differential equation of transfer into a pure integral equation using the majorant transmittance. Choose this variant when media density varies significantly along rays and standard tracking becomes inefficient.
 
